  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, honestly, I'm only sitting here because my husband basically forced me to come. He and, well, all the people down at the warehouse where I work, they keep acting like I'm crazy or something. Like I'm just making things up out of thin air. But I'm not. I've been moving freight there for a long time, and I know exactly what's going on. \n\nSee, they have been watching my every move. I can feel them staring when I'm out on the floor. And it's not just looking—they are actively messing with my work. I'll load up a pallet, right? Get it all wrapped, count the boxes, log it in. I know my numbers, I'm good at my job. But then I'll walk away for two seconds to grab the pallet jack, and when I check the system later, the pallet counts are changed. They are deliberately going into the system and changing my numbers behind my back! \n\nAnd I know exactly why they're doing it, too. There’s a supervisor spot opening up, and I’ve been working my tail off for it, so they’re doing all this... this sabotage. Changing my counts and watching me from the racks, just to make me look bad so they can keep me from getting that supervisor spot. And instead of backing me up, my husband just takes their side and says I need to see a doctor. So, that's why I'm here. Even though I'm the only one actually paying attention to what they're doing to me.",
