    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "That sounds like a very stressful experience to go through. How long have you been noticing these things happening at work?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it’s been a while now. I’d say, if I really think back on it, it’s been about eight months. Yeah, eight months of this constant... this constant feeling of being watched, and the numbers being messed with. And, you know, it’s not just the staring and the pallets, either. There are the voices, too. I started hearing them right around the same time, about eight months ago. \n\nAt first, I thought it was just the warehouse noise, you know? It’s loud in there—forklifts beeping, the big bay doors rattling, people shouting across the floor. But then I realized the voices weren't coming from the floor. They were, like, right there, talking about me. Whispering about how I was messing up, or how I wasn't going to get the promotion. And it’s just been going on and on for eight whole months. Every single shift, I go in there, and I have to deal with the eyes on me, the system getting hacked to change my counts, and those voices just chiming in. \n\nAnd my husband, he thinks I'm just stressed because of the supervisor spot, but how can I not be stressed when this has been my life for eight months? I mean, anybody would be on edge if they had to deal with that kind of sabotage day in and day out for that long. It’s exhausting, it really is. I just want to do my job and get what I earned, but they’ve been at this for eight months straight, just trying to break me down.",
