    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these past eight months, have you had periods where you felt persistently down, sad, or depressed most of the day?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, no, I haven't been sad. I mean, sure, I get frustrated, obviously. Like I said, who wouldn't be frustrated when people are constantly messing with your work and changing your numbers? It makes you want to pull your hair out! But sad? Depressed? No, definitely not. I haven't been sitting around crying or moping or anything like that. \n\nIf anything, I've just been angry. And determined. I am so determined to prove that I am doing my job right, you know? I go into that warehouse every day, and I keep my head up, and I do my work, even with all the whispering and the staring. I don't let them see me down. I don't have time to be depressed. I have to stay sharp, because if I don't pay attention for even a second, that's when they sneak into the system. So, no, I'm not depressed. I'm just tired of the sabotage. My husband keeps trying to say I'm acting depressed, but he just doesn't get it. He doesn't see what I have to deal with every single day on that floor. He just sits in his office all day, he has no idea what it's like to have people actively trying to ruin your life for eight months straight. So, no, definitely not sad. Just... fed up. Extremely fed up with the whole situation.",
